VITA-WW-17 host hook: where the captured GX stream and the guest's present
events reach the renderer. Apply with `git apply` (verified against 8d50556);
this file is delivered as a patch, not committed to the renderer branch.

What it does:
  - builds the renderer (vita/renderer) into the host: C++ enabled, the pinned
    RetailGxFrontend/gxcore enabled, ww_renderer linked into ww05_services (so
    every probe gets it) and the Vita link line given vitaGL + the Cg stubs.
    Use the same no-splash vitaGL archive the WW02 launcher pins.
  - creates the renderer after ww_host_init over the host's own memory view
    and destroys it in ww_host_shutdown.
  - hands every completed captured GX command to ww_renderer_write and calls
    ww_renderer_present after it. The present call shows a frame exactly when a
    display copy completed one; move it to the march's VI/present site when
    that exists.
  - reports what the renderer saw: a RENDER line between STOP and END and a
    real rendered=<presented frames> in END, with scripts/vita/ww05/report.py
    accepting the new shape (its PASS/STOP-reason conditions stay the march's).

Not in this patch (the march's lane): continuing past the first complete GX
command, the VI retrace clock, and the [frame-timing]/[frame-present] markers.

